Title: The Last Bus
Credit: Written by
Author: Previz Stage
Draft date: 2026-10-24

EXT. CITY STREET - NIGHT

Rain-slick asphalt shines under sodium streetlights. Shuttered storefronts, a bus shelter with a flickering ad panel, puddles on the kerb.

MAYA (30s, denim jacket over a yellow hoodie, box braids) waits at the kerb, checking her phone. A red sedan drives past, its headlights sweeping the shop shutters.

THEO (40s, tall, rumpled tan raincoat, salt-and-pepper stubble) hurries up beside her, out of breath.

THEO
You missed the last bus too?

MAYA
(without looking up)
I let it go. I wasn't ready to go home.

THEO
That's the saddest thing I've heard all week.

MAYA
It's Tuesday.

A night bus rumbles by without stopping. They both watch it go.

INT. KITCHEN - MORNING

Pale sunlight through a window over the sink. Mismatched mugs on open shelves, a small wooden table with two chairs, a kettle on the stove.

Maya sits at the table. Theo stands by the stove in his socks. The kettle starts to whistle.

THEO
Coffee or tea?

MAYA
Whatever you're having.

THEO
(pouring)
I'm having both. It's been that kind of night.

MAYA
You really don't sleep, do you?

EXT. ROOFTOP - DUSK

A tar-paper rooftop ringed by a low brick parapet. Water towers silhouetted against an orange sky, the city skyline beyond. Pigeons circle overhead.

Maya leans on the parapet. Theo joins her, two mugs in hand.

MAYA
From up here it all looks fixable.

THEO
Most things do, from far enough away.

MAYA
Then let's stay up here a while.

THEO
(handing her a mug)
Deal.

FADE OUT.
